# Commercial boundary (Core)

Paid connectors live in **canary-commercial**, not this repo.

## Never do in Core

- New Alembic revisions for Casera / HMLR / DocuSign / SDLT / search-provider tables or columns
- Product UI under `frontend/src` (AdminCasera, MatterSdltPanel, etc.)
- Connector routers under `backend/app/routers/*{casera,hmlr,docusign,sdlt,searches}*`
- Resurrect deleted `app.docusign_*` / `app.casera_*` / `app.hmlr_*` shims

## Do this instead

| Change | Put it in |
|--------|-----------|
| New vendor DDL | `canary-commercial/module/migrations/versions/00N_*.sql` |
| Routers / clients / services | `canary-commercial/python/canary_commercial/` |
| Admin / matter UI | `canary-commercial/module/ui/` + `module/manifest.json` slot |

Core may only add **slot hosts**, menu chrome, and thin re-exports. Historical Alembic vendor files listed in `scripts/check_commercial_boundary.py` are frozen — do not add to that allow-list.

Before finishing vendor-related work, run:

```bash
python3 scripts/check_commercial_boundary.py
```

See `docs/COMMERCIAL_PACKAGE.md` and `backend/alembic/COMMERCIAL_SCHEMA.md`.
